    "why": "Four lifting days of 60 min: upper/lower, full body A/B twice and A/B/C/D are all built; A/B twice trains the same muscles hard on consecutive days, upper/lower misses the quads priority, and A/B/C/D wins on the recomposition goal, the posture emphasis and the skip risk. With no priority muscles in the profile, the recomposition goal makes upper back, lats (the posture emphasis) and quads the priorities. Five strict pull-ups put pull-ups in as the main vertical pull (ladder level 6), the 60 s plank starts the core ladder at hollow holds, 30 s balance brings rear-foot-elevated split squats in, the overhead reach keeps overhead pressing out, and the three 30-min short days carry the chosen cardio modes, intervals included."
